{-
   The bare name a `data qualified` takes away.

   The accepting half is `QualifiedData.yana`, and this is the sentence it cannot say: a constructor
   of a qualified record is not in the module's namespace, so writing it bare is an unknown name
   rather than a name that resolves to the wrong thing. Both stages once reported it identically,
   which was the point - the ownership stage read the flag nowhere at all until 2026-09-05 and
   accepted every bare name, which is how `lib/Date/Format.yana`'s two enums came to collide.

   A **newtype** is deliberately not here. `alias qualified` writes the same word and means the form
   rather than the namespace, so `StringId(4)` stays legal and `Newtype.yana` asserts it.
-}

data qualified Unit = Nanos | Micros

fn main() -> Int = match Nanos:
    Unit.Nanos: 1
    Unit.Micros: 2
